WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.768
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.000
NARRATOR: Traffic signal
poles must be strong enough

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.330
to bear the weight of
road signs, street lights,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.870
and, of course, traffic signals.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.310
The poles are also
built to withstand

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.940
extreme weather conditions,
such as high winds

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.058
and heavy snow accumulation.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.130
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.520
Traffic signal poles are
made of high strength steel.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.400
Years of weather exposure
can cause corrosion,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.550
so the poles are galvanized
on both sides for protection.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.730
Each pole has a welded
plate to connect

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.230
it to a perpendicular pole.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.530
The poles are made out
of these steel sheets.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.950
The steel arrives at the
factory in one large roll.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:53.000
They use a decoiler to unwind
the sheet and flatten it out.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.340
Then, as shear cuts it
to the correct length.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.230
A computer-guided plasma
cutter marks short lines

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:03.550
on both ends of the sheet.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.780
These lines indicate where
to bend the flat sheet

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:09.100
to form a round pole.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.560
The machine cuts the sheet
into a rectangular shape

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.800
or a trapezoid shape, if the
pole will taper at the top.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.670
Workers number of the
machine lines with chalk,

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.790
giving lines directly opposite
of each other the same number.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.680
Then, they transfer the
sheet to a bending machine

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:32.700
called a press break.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.676
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.040
The press break bends the
sheet along the marked line

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.750
to a pre-programmed angle.

00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.820
Workers use a digital
measuring device

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.252
to make sure the first
bend is accurate.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.550
If it is, they continue
bending along the remainder

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.370
of the lines, transforming
the flat sheet

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.350
into a multisided round pole.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.280
Now, the poll moves
to a welding station

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.920
where hydraulic rollers apply
pressure from both sides.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.590
This forces the
edges of the sheet

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:19.080
together so that a
welding head can fuse

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.300
the seam with molten steel.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.690
At the same time, the head
deposits a granular powder

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.020
called flux, which prevents
air from penetrating the weld

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:28.860
and weakening it.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.800
Workers place the pole
in a hydraulic press,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.800
so it doesn't warp as the
seam weld cools and shrinks.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:45.410
Next, a computer-guided plasma
machine cuts a connection

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.445
played out of thick steel.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.810
The machine also drills
holes for the high strength

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.930
bolts needed to attach the plate
to the traffic signal pole.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.510
Workers center the
connection plate on support

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.400
plates they've already
welded to the pole.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.080
Then, they weld
everything in place.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.647
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.380
Next, workers weld a base plate
to the bottom of the pole.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.180
It has holes for
the anchor bolts

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.940
which are used for securing the
traffic signal to the street.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.590
Workers inspect the welds
with a testing device.

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:33.650
It uses an electric current
to magnetically draw colored

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.650
powder into any defective area.

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.860
The factory ships
the finished poles

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.140
to a galvanizing plant
where they're dipped

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.700
in a series of wash tanks.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:49.750
The plants' tanks are deep
enough to fully submerge

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.260
the poles so they can treat
both the inner and outer surface

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.210
at the same time.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.730
Now, the poles go into
a vat of sulfuric acid.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.490
This bath dissolves the
more stubborn contaminants

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:04.690
that washing can't remove.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:09.040
The next tank contains
a chemical that weakens

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.130
the surface of the poles.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.230
This allows the galvanizing
metal to penetrate the steel

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.475
rather than sit on the surface.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.810
The final tank
contains molten zinc.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:23.650
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:29.570
As the poles bathe in
the 842 degree zinc,

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:31.820
workers in fire
protection suits skim

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:35.720
the surface to remove iron oxide
and ash that floats to the top.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:39.970
This keeps the freshly
galvanized surface

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:43.480
clean as the poles are
hoisted out of the tank

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.890
and set aside to cool.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:49.170
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.930
Because they're galvanized
rather than painted,

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.940
these polls are able
to support traffic

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.230
lights, signs, and street
lamps for 40 years or more.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:02.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

